  "content": "Approach play is where the team loses the most strokes, and putting is second.\n\nThe season read has a coverage problem. It covers only 11 rounds from one player, between August 21 and October 21. In that window the team averages -4.37 strokes per round on approach and -2.4 on putting. Off the tee is -1.36 and around the green is 0.07. These are measured against a Tour baseline of 0. There is no college figure for strokes gained.\n\nBecause the season read is that thin, I checked each player's newest ten rounds. That covers 55 rounds by 7 players, from May 29 to October 21. It gives the same order. Approach is -3.09 per round and putting is -3.03. Around the green is -0.1, and off the tee is the only area above baseline at 0.4.\n\nTreat approach and putting as the two leaks. Approach is clearly ahead on the season figure, but the two are close on the broader ten-round read. Audit Testplayer has no recorded rounds. Six other players have rounds but no season strokes gained, so only one player's figures are in the season read. I can break either leak down by player or by distance band if you want.",
